@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:1000
@CO	Records for queries/strand/dnmtools.toml
@CO	queries/strand/dnmtools.toml -- the original strand is CV combined with 0x10, not CV alone: a T-rich read mapped reverse reads G>A against the reference. SEQ must be repaired first; see the rule file.
@CO	Each QNAME is the call the rule must make for that record: "<original>:<aligned>",
@CO	each side forward or reverse, or "unknown". Anything after the first "/" is a label
@CO	for the reader. The test that enforces it is in src/strand_rule.rs.
